  "notes": "The party-country centre — \"the most programmed rhythm section of the pre-2015 radio cohort.\" The drums are the entry's list, not a paraphrase: \"'syncopated drum loops,' programmed claps on the backbeat, 16th shaker/hat loops, sampled kicks under the live kick, and full stop-time drops. Verses often run on the loop alone with the live kit entering at the chorus.\" The 808 block is authored in the `counter_riff` role because the entry describes two distinct layers doing two distinct jobs — \"on the party cuts the sub carries beats 1 and 3 with the electric bass playing the syncopated figure above it\" — so the sub is a downbeat lane and the live bass keeps the syncopation, which is why `bassline.anticipationProb` is high while the 808 is short and slide-free. Harmony is the stated \"I–V–vi–IV and I–IV–V, with vi–IV–I–V on the ballads.\" Melody is \"high-tenor with a falsetto hook in the post-chorus, syncopated 16th-note phrasing in the verses,\" hence the high density with `straightEighthsProb` pushed down. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: high-medium); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF] and songdata's 130–172 figures fold onto the low end of the stated band. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the 808 register, the clap offsets and the counter ratio.",
